  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.7,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U1"],
      "pins": ["U1.5"],
      "nets": ["I2C_SCL_FCC", "I2C2_SCL_FCC"],
      "observed": "On the Power sheet the INA219 (U1) SDA pin 6 is on net I2C2_SDA_FCC, but its SCL pin 5 is on a net labelled 'I2C_SCL_FCC' (no bus number). That net name does not appear on any other pin anywhere in the drawing: the FCC MCU's I2C2 clock pin and the I2C2 pull-up resistor are both on 'I2C2_SCL_FCC'. The INA219 clock line is therefore left floating / not connected to the MCU.",
      "expected": "The INA219 is an I2C device that must be clocked; its SCL pin should share the same I2C bus net as its SDA pin (I2C2_SCL_FCC), per the spec which places the INA219 on the I2C interface and lists it as a working 'Voltage/Current/Power Sense IC'.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Power sheet, U1 INA21AIDCNR: pin 6 box 'I2C2_SDA_FCC', pin 5 box 'I2C_SCL_FCC'"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "FCC sheet, FCC1 STM32H753VITx pin label 'I2C2_SCL_FCC' and 'I2C Pull-Up Resistors' block net 'I2C2_SCL_FCC' (no 'I2C_SCL_FCC' net exists elsewhere)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "INA219AIDCNR, I2C addr 0x40, across R1 = 10 mΩ shunt ... 'Voltage/Current/Power Sense IC'"}
      ],
      "impact": "The INA219 receives no clock, so the battery current/voltage/power telemetry is dead; the MCU cannot read the sensor at all.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U2"],
      "pins": ["U2.1"],
      "nets": ["I2C2_SCL_FCC", "I2C2_SDA_FCC"],
      "observed": "On the FCC Peripherals sheet the PWM driver U2 (PCA9685PW) carries the note 'I2C address: 0x41' and its A0 pin (pin 1) is tied to +3.3V while A1–A5 are tied to GND, giving the 0x41 address. It is wired onto the same I2C2 bus as the INA219.",
      "expected": "The specification states the PWM/servo driver is at I2C address 0x40 ('NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40').",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "FCC Peripherals sheet, U2 PCA9685PW: 'I2C address: 0x41', A0 pin 1 to +3.3V, SCL pin 26 = I2C2_SCL_FCC, SDA pin 27 = I2C2_SDA_FCC"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "PWM/servo driver | FCCPeripherals | NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40"}
      ],
      "impact": "Software/firmware that addresses the servo driver at the intended 0x40 will not find it on the bus, so PWM servo output control fails.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing deviates from the intended design in the I2C interface of the FCC-local peripherals: the INA219's SCL pin is on a stray 'I2C_SCL_FCC' net that no MCU pin or pull-up drives (open clock line), and the PCA9685 PWM driver is configured to address 0x41 instead of the specified 0x40. The documented barometer RESET/EOC swap is a known bug and was not reported."
}

